    "onboardingIntro1": "EcoZones are neighborhoods that promote collaboration, sustainability, and prosperity. This app will help you identify the challenges and opportunities in your neighborhood across four dimensions: urban environment, environmental quality, socioeconomic well-being, and disaster risk.",
    "onboardingIntro2": "Complete the neighborhood survey and collaborative mapping to identify these challenges. The results will generate a report for your neighborhood, prioritizing Sustainable Urban Solutions (SUS) of short-term and low-cost implementation that can be applied in your community. You can view and download this report on the website: www.ecozonas.org, along with other resources and a catalogue of Sustainable Urban Solutions.",
    "onboardingIntro3": "For a complete assessment, follow these steps:",
    "onboarding1": "Complete the survey and encourage others to do it as well.",
    "onboarding2": "Map the challenges and opportunities in your neighborhood and submit the information.",
    "onboarding3": "Download the report with the diagnosis and solutions from the website www.ecozonas.org.",
    "aboutEcozonas": "About EcoZonas",
    "@aboutEcozonas": {"description": "Bottom navigation tab. EcoZonas is the project name; do not translate it."},
    "onboardingOutro": "This tool is part of the \"EcoZones\" project, implemented by WRI Mexico and the Wuppertal Institute, supported by the German Federal Ministry for Economic Affairs and Climate Action and the International Climate Initiative (IKI).",
    "goToTools": "Go to tools",
    "@goToTools": {"description": "Button at the end of the onboarding that opens the diagnostic tools."},
    "moreInfoIntro": "Visit www.ecozonas.org from your computer to view the results of the survey and mapping conducted in your community and other regions. On the website, you will find information on:",
    "moreInfo1": "Survey: Check the survey results in your neighborhood, focusing on the main challenges and opportunities. Additionally, you will find a prioritization of Sustainable Urban Solutions (SUS) with proposed interventions for your neighborhood based on the identified challenges.",
    "moreInfo2": "Mapping: Explore the map of all mapped objects and a summary of the evaluation of your community.",
    "moreInfo3": "Catalog of Sustainable Urban Solutions (SUS): Filter solutions according to the identified challenges or explore the catalog with 160 ideas to implement in your neighborhood.",
    "moreInfo4": "Download the report with the diagnosis of your neighborhood and the prioritized SUS, as well as the databases with the collected information.",
    "moreInfo5": "Visit www.ecozonas.org and invite others to check it out!",
