    "urbanEnvironment": "Urban environment",
    "urbanEnvironmentText": "The urban environment includes the elements that are part of a neighborhood: public spaces such as parks, squares and green areas; public transportation, pedestrian streets, and bike lanes; schools, health centers, shops, and more. An adequate urban environment is attractive, safe, inclusive, and environmentally friendly.",
    "disasterRisk": "Disaster risk",
    "disasterRiskText": "The disaster risk dimension refers to negative effects and impacts on people, homes, and businesses that a neighborhood may face from natural phenomena and disasters, such as floods, heatwaves, or fires. A community that prepares for these risks can take measure to protect and recover.",
    "environmentalQuality": "Environmental quality",
    "environmentalQualityText": "The environmental characteristics of a neighborhood include practices and situations that impact the quality of the environment and the health of the population. For example, this refers to air or water cleanliness, waste management, or the presence of pollution in the neighborhood.",
    "socioeconomicWellbeing": "Socioeconomic Wellbeing",
    "socioeconomicWellbeingText": "Socioeconomic well-being refers to the opportunities for employment, education, information, and health that people have access to. It also includes participation in income-generating activities and events that foster a sense of community.",
